            <ArticleTitle>[The analgesic effect of interference currents in radicular pains].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>235-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors tried out the analgetic effectiveness of interference currents generated by an Interdyn--ID 79 unit of Polish production in the treatment of radicular pains caused by disc prolapse. The analgesic effect, its degree and duration were assessed. In 72% of cases a good analgesic effect was obtained lasting at least one month, and in 35% of cases complete remission of pain was was achieved. It is stressed that the obtained effects were similar to those obtained by other methods of nervous system electrostimulation, such as: percutaneous electrostimulation, electroacupuncture, spinal cord electrostimulation, or diadynamic currents.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
